  "system": {
    "biography": "<p>The colony's labour caste in a human host — tending cocoons and larvae. <strong>It has no printed attack at all</strong> and is not a combatant: it screeches to warn the Hive and will throw itself in front of a blow to protect the cocoons or the Queen.</p><p><strong>This replaces the old 'Worker Ant Spirit (Flesh Form, Force 3)'.</strong> The printed Worker is Force 1, so an existing token becomes weaker than the GM expected, not stronger.</p><p><strong>Manual rules the sheet does not enforce.</strong> Powers and Weaknesses are not fields on the NPC data model, so they live here as prose. Switching these to <code>spirit</code> actors would be worse — <code>SpiritData.prepareDerivedData</code> recomputes attributes from Force and would overwrite the printed table this whole audit exists to restore.</p><p><strong>Astral:</strong> add <strong>+5 Initiative</strong> when acting astrally (the printed Reaction shows this as the bracketed second value). It is deliberately NOT baked into <code>reaction</code>, which would also inflate dodge and defence.</p><p><strong>Attack:</strong> None Physical (printed SR1 <code>None</code>, converted by p.283 method B — no SR2 item is an ant's mandibles, so the staging digit folds into Power).</p><p><strong>Powers:</strong> Enhanced Senses (Smell).<br><strong>Weaknesses:</strong> Reduced Senses (Sight).</p><p><em>Queen Euphoria p.47, transcribed from a 300 dpi render.</em></p>",
